`reverseBuiltInUrlTagMap` is rebuilt via `Object.fromEntries` + `Object.entries` + `.map` on every call to `serializeTagsParam`. Since `BUILT_IN_URL_TAG_MAP` is a module-level constant, the reverse map can also be a module-level constant:

```ts
const REVERSE_BUILT_IN_URL_TAG_MAP: Record<string, string> = Object.fromEntries(
  Object.entries(BUILT_IN_URL_TAG_MAP).map(([urlTag, internalTag]) => [internalTag, urlTag])
);
```

This avoids allocating objects on every serialization call.
